# Slice 19's verification, as a file instead of as a memory.
#
# Picking into an inset pane was the latent bug that slice existed to find, and
# it was checked by hand: screenshot, read a sphere's coordinates off the image,
# click there, screenshot again, compare by eye. This is that check, repeatable.
#
# Run it:  cargo xtask shoot workspace --script capture/workspace.script
#
# Frame numbers, not seconds. The engine holds on each one, so a click lands on a
# known frame and the ring is in a known position — which is what makes the
# coordinates below stable rather than a guess about timing.

# Frame 150: the scene inset between two panels. The reference shot.
150  shot  inset

# Stop the ring, so the props stay where the shot above found them. The "turning"
# checkbox is in the left panel, and panel geometry comes from the theme's own
# metrics, so this coordinate is as stable as the layout is.
200  move  76 175
200  click

# Frame 260: paused, and the props are parked. This is what the click below aims
# at, and the pair (parked, selected) is what a diff should show a cage between.
260  shot  parked

# Click the cyan sphere. If `pointer_ray` ever goes back to unprojecting through
# the whole window instead of the scene rect, this misses it — which is exactly
# the regression worth catching, and exactly the one no compile check can.
300  move  414 368
300  click
340  shot  selected

# And a click on the left panel, which must NOT reach the scene. It toggles the
# theme instead; the selection above has to survive it.
400  move  128 250
400  click
440  shot  panel-click
